From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] shell: the Space keys must work from every shell window

F7 did not return from the modern Space to the classic one whenever the
Settings control panel was open, and the panel could not be dismissed
either - no shell key worked at all while it had focus. Verified: with the
panel up, F3, F7 and Escape produce no "GTK4 semantic key event" line, so
the shell never saw them.

The chain:

1. jarabe/main.py runs `metacity-message disable-keybindings` at startup,
   so the window manager owns no keys. The Metacity keybinding the Spaces
   controller writes (switch-to-workspace-1 = ['F7']) can never fire, and
   clearing it changes nothing. Every global key must come from the shell.
2. F7/F8 were handled by a capture controller bolted onto _main_window,
   _overlay and stack in main.py, not by the shell's key handler, so they
   were bound to that one window.
3. ControlPanel is a plain Gtk.Window built without `application=`, so it
   never joins the Gtk.Application, 'window-added' never fires, and
   KeyHandler.add_window() never attached its controller.

So while the control panel was focused nothing listened for F7, and the
classic Space had already released its own grab - correctly, that is what
lets the modern Space own F1-F8 at all.

Give the Space keys a single owner in _actions_table, drop the duplicate
in main.py, and register the control panel with the key handler it was
missing. The modal gate keeps working as before: F1-F6 are in
_non_modal_action_keys and stay suppressed while the panel is up, while
F7/F8 are not, so leaving the Space keeps working.

Registering the window with the handler is deliberately not the same as
adding it to the application: ShellModel._window_added_cb would turn a
new application window into a phantom entry in the activity list.

--- a/src/jarabe/view/keyhandler.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/view/keyhandler.py
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 import os
 import logging
 import importlib
+import subprocess
 import types
 
 from gi.repository import GLib
@@ -66,7 +67,12 @@
     '<alt><shift>m': 'open_controlpanel',
     '<alt><shift>o': 'open_search',
     '<alt><shift>q': 'logout',
-    '<alt><shift>d': 'dump_ui_tree'
+    '<alt><shift>d': 'dump_ui_tree',
+    # Aspartame Spaces. Sugar disables every window manager keybinding at
+    # startup, so nothing outside the shell can switch workspaces: these
+    # have to be shell actions like the rest of the table.
+    'F7': 'space_classic',
+    'F8': 'space_modern',
 }
 
 # These keys will not be trigger a action if a modal dialog is opened
@@ -234,6 +240,18 @@
             panel.set_transient_for(shell_model._main_window)
         panel.set_visible(True)
 
+    def _switch_space(self, target):
+        controller = os.environ.get(
+            'ASPARTAME_SPACE_SWITCHER',
+            '/mnt/aspartame-dev/scripts/sugar-gtk4-space.sh')
+        subprocess.Popen([controller, target], close_fds=True)
+
+    def handle_space_classic(self, event_time):
+        self._switch_space('gtk3')
+
+    def handle_space_modern(self, event_time):
+        self._switch_space('gtk4')
+
     def handle_dump_ui_tree(self, event_time):
         if uitree:
             print(uitree.get_root().dump())
